  "details": "Users can see their own tracking scale(how big the world appears relative to unity scale) inside of the debug menu(right shift+`+3). This only applies to that specific avatar. Allowing this in udon would make it so that world creators can make things for certain scales of avatar. Or enforce a 1 to 1 or close size avatar for certain games. Alternatively there could be a way to scale users avatars inside udon, but thats a bit out of the scope of this question.",
